  "passage": "Grandma used a voice assistant to set timers, play music, and call family members. She liked it because typing on a phone was hard for her.\nOne day, the device misunderstood her and ordered twelve bags of rice online. The family laughed, cancelled the order, and changed the settings.\nGrandma still used the assistant, but she learned to check important actions before confirming them.\nThe family also talked about privacy. The device had to listen for commands, but how much should people allow it to hear?\nThe voice assistant was useful, but it brought questions with it. Convenience often comes with settings that need attention.",
